Label-free baseline

RoBERTa large fine-tuned on MNLI (`roberta-large-mnli`), run locally as a label-free
inference baseline (see `accord/differential/nli_baseline.py`), is used under the terms
of its model card.

Public benchmark and survey data used by the public control experiments:
- SNLI, the Stanford Natural Language Inference corpus (Bowman et al., 2015), Stanford NLP Group.
- AG News topic classification data (Zhang, Zhao and LeCun, 2015), derived from the AG corpus of news articles.
- American Community Survey Public Use Microdata Sample (PUMS), U.S. Census Bureau.
Each is used under the terms published by its provider. For AG News and the PUMS this repository commits only
row indices, labels, hashes, model scores and aggregate statistics derived from them, not the corpus text.

SNLI is the exception: corpus text is committed. `accord/prevalence_replication/data/snli_test.parquet` and
`accord/prevalence_replication/data/snli_validation.parquet` are the SNLI test and validation splits (10,000 rows
each; columns `premise`, `hypothesis`, `label`), unmodified, as downloaded from the Hugging Face mirror named in
`accord/prevalence_replication/build_pools.py` (huggingface.co/datasets/stanfordnlp/snli). No file in this
repository other than this one records SNLI's licence. The dataset card at that address, read on 18 September
2026, states: "The Stanford Natural Language Inference Corpus by The Stanford NLP Group is licensed under a
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License. The corpus includes content from the
Flickr 30k corpus, also released under an Attribution-ShareAlike licence." The two parquet files are
redistributed here under that licence (CC BY-SA 4.0), which is not the licence of this repository's own code.
Attribution: Samuel R. Bowman, Gabor Angeli, Christopher Potts and Christopher D. Manning, "A large annotated
corpus for learning natural language inference", EMNLP 2015.

HANS, the Heuristic Analysis for NLI Systems evaluation set (McCoy, Pavlick and Linzen, 2019; cited as
`mccoy2019hans`), is vendored in full at `accord/public_controls/nlifactorial/data/heuristics_evaluation_set.txt`,
downloaded once from the official McCoy repository, per `accord/public_controls/nlifactorial/build_manifest.py`
and `C104_PREREGISTRATION.md`. Those files record it as MIT licensed; no separate LICENSE file or header ships
with the vendored copy in this repository.
